WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.200
Let’s walk through Responses.

00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:05.775
Separate White Cell rulings, update notices, forwarded items

00:00:05.775 --> 00:00:07.662
, and general communications.

00:00:07.662 --> 00:00:10.812
Bring material information back into the owning team workflow before

00:00:10.812 --> 00:00:12.850
changing a durable artifact.

00:00:12.850 --> 00:00:15.900
On this slide, follow White Cell answers, updates

00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:18.212
, and inbound operational messages.

00:00:18.212 --> 00:00:22.050
In practice, treat explicit White Cell responses as exercise

00:00:22.050 --> 00:00:24.775
input while preserving the observer boundary.

00:00:24.775 --> 00:00:27.525
When you are ready, use Open Responses to move

00:00:27.525 --> 00:00:28.938
to the live surface.

00:00:29.435 --> 00:00:32.110
The guide will not make the workflow decision for you

00:00:32.110 --> 00:00:32.285
.
